    "statement_raw_token": "\"Let ${\\\\goth M}:=\\\\VerSpace(k,\\\\PolarSpace(\\\\varpi))$, and let ${\\\\mathscr H}$ be a hyperplane of $\\\\VerSpace(k,\\\\text{\\\\boldmath$\\\\goth P$})$ determined by a polarity $\\\\varkappa$. The intersection\\n\\n$$\\n{\\\\mathscr H}\\\\cap{\\\\mathfrak y}_k(Q_0(\\\\varpi))\\n$$\\n\\nis a hyperplane in ${\\\\goth M}$. **Hyperplane classification conjecture.** The hyperplanes of ${\\\\goth M}$ are precisely those of the form\\n\\n$$\\n{\\\\mathscr H}\\\\cap{\\\\mathfrak y}_k(Q_0(\\\\varpi)).\\n$$\\n\\nThe claim proposes a complete description of the hyperplanes in the Veronese space associated with a polar space; the source gives no proof, so its status remains open.\"",
    "statement_raw_token_sha256": "c5828d92372c317c442ec76bb8f644e44014974d92640e5a4d9590b82447bdd7",
