    "statement_raw_token": "\"Let $G$ be a simple connected graph with $n$ vertices, and let $\\\\operatorname{irr}_{t}(G)$ denote its total irregularity. A graph is **regular** if all its vertices have the same degree. **Second-minimal total irregularity conjecture.** If $G$ is not a regular graph, then\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\operatorname{irr}_{t}(G)\\\\geq 2n-4.\\n$$\\n\\nThe paper identifies $0$ as the minimal total irregularity, attained by regular graphs, and proposes $2n-4$ as the second-minimal value for simple connected graphs on $n$ vertices. The claim is presented as an open problem for further research.\"",
    "statement_raw_token_sha256": "13086b8f9f0ecefa7b5727fcabf39a01493fa0a572ddf960f48ba920f34c9ef2",
    "statement_decoded_utf8_sha256": "004b23230105944153409890edceab03b9d0e1314b1343b3af081e79ede1768d",
    "statement_decoded_utf8_bytes": 561
