    "statement_raw_token": "\"Let $G$ be an isolate-free forest of order $n$. In the domination game, Dominator starts in $Dominator-start game$, whose game domination number is denoted by $\\\\gamma_g(G)$, while $\\\\gamma_g'(G)$ denotes the corresponding Staller-start game number.\\n\\n**Kinnersley\u2013West\u2013Zamani 3/5-conjecture.**\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\gamma_g(G) \\\\leq \\\\frac{3n}{5}\\\\quad\\\\text{and}\\\\quad \\\\gamma_g'(G) \\\\leq \\\\frac{3n+2}{5}.\\n$$\\n\\nThis conjecture proposes the sharp upper bounds for the two domination-game variants on isolate-free forests; the paper presents it as an open problem.\"",
    "statement_raw_token_sha256": "3aa0c5b99855122b31eedd9a76c3b0273119b11ef0cacdb617b3c62308951af6",
    "statement_decoded_utf8_sha256": "2f3e723e54270bb4897cd5691f129610793ea572b23c042567c329a17363c5f0",
