    "statement_raw_token": "\"Let $C\\\\subset\\\\mathbb{C}P^2$ be a rational cuspidal curve of degree $d$ with $\\\\nu$ cusps and let $F$ be the function defined from the semigroup counting functions of its singularities as in the alternative combinatorial form. **First index-theoretic alternative conjecture.** Under these conditions,\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\sum_{j=0}^{d-3}F(jd)\\\\leq\\\\sum_{j=0}^{d-3}\\\\frac{(j+1)(j+2)}{2}=\\\\frac{d(d-1)(d-2)}{6}.\\n$$\\n\\nThis is obtained by summing the coefficientwise inequalities and is therefore weaker than the alternative combinatorial conjecture. It is part of the same open conjectural package, although the paper proves the stronger statement for two cusps.\"",
    "statement_raw_token_sha256": "8ce5e3b1561d74de44361da6c6fb84d24187e88867bdf439b2d8941e56b95483",
    "statement_decoded_utf8_sha256": "bff0987d5c52cbb84e6e90f98d2d514e56dfe5d073ca6f915f122f7c67d5315b",
