    "statement_raw_token": "\"Let $p>2$ and let $f:GF(p)^n\\\\to GF(p)$ be a weakly regular bent function corresponding to a weighted strongly regular graph via the stated analogy. Let $\\\\mu_{ii}$ denote the diagonal intersection number for the associated weighted partial difference set, for $1\\\\leq i\\\\leq s$. **Walsh's conjecture.** One has\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\mu_{ii}=0,\\\\qquad 1\\\\leq i\\\\leq s.\\n$$\\n\\nThis predicts a structural restriction on the weighted partial difference set associated with a weakly regular bent function and its weighted strongly regular graph. The supplied text gives no resolution, so the conjecture remains open.\"",
    "statement_raw_token_sha256": "0b755cebc0f81552f3176adbb6c12decbfbb10397667864bd9544ce28632a997",
