    "statement_raw_token": "\"Let $G$ be a graph, let $k\\\\in\\\\mathbb{Z}^+$, and let $D$ be a **$k$-optimal set**, meaning a $k$-dependent set maximizing $\\\\phi_k(D)=k|D|-|E(G[D])|$. A subgraph is **$k$-edge-chromatic** if its edges can be coloured with $k$ colours so that adjacent edges receive different colours. **The $k$-optimal set edge-colouring conjecture.** If $D$ is a $k$-optimal set in $G$, then $G$ has a $k$-edge-chromatic subgraph in which every vertex of $V(G)-D$ has degree $k$.\\n\\nThis conjecture is introduced as a natural strengthening of the results developed earlier and is stated to imply the special case of Tuza's conjecture for graphs of the form $I_k\\\\vee H$. Its resolution is not supplied in the source.\"",
    "statement_raw_token_sha256": "eaeccc1a4e06996ee5987a9f99da7c7e82cad06b085232d393ba468f3bbb13e9",
    "statement_decoded_utf8_sha256": "b834bb1568668448e8a6fe91424cdf059890c6d90d5c5b8c38cc5454348ec8ad",
    "statement_decoded_utf8_bytes": 695
