    "statement_raw_token": "\"Let $\\\\mathcal{U}\\\\subseteq\\\\operatorname{AG}(2,q)$ be a maximal affine set, let $\\\\mathcal{D}$ be the set of directions determined by $\\\\mathcal{U}$, and let $s$ and $t$ be the associated parameters.\\n\\n**Maximal affine-set linearity conjecture.** If $t=s>2$, then $\\\\mathcal{U}$ is an affine $\\\\operatorname{GF}(s)$-linear set.\\n\\nThe conjecture proposes linearity for maximal affine sets in the case $s=t>2$, following examples of maximal affine sets that are not linear when $s=1$. The supplied text gives no resolution, so the conjecture remains open.\"",
    "statement_raw_token_sha256": "ed16bbf62b5748a36a6ead21ea33b605cf8c22a3ca4e22f16b73f98e73a4c814",
