    "statement_raw_token": "\"Let $G$ be a connected graph with $n$ vertices, $m$ edges, eigenvalues $\\\\lambda_1,\\\\ldots,\\\\lambda_n$ of its adjacency matrix, graph energy $E=\\\\sum_{i=1}^n|\\\\lambda_i|$, and vertex degrees $d_1,\\\\ldots,d_n$. Define\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\epsilon=\\\\frac{n\\\\sum_{i\\\\sim j}\\\\sqrt{d_i d_j}}{2m^2}.\\n$$\\n\\n**Elphick's conjecture.** The graph energy satisfies\\n\\n$$\\nE\\\\geq\\\\frac{n}{\\\\epsilon}.\\n$$\\n\\nThis conjecture was communicated by Clive Elphick and would improve the known lower bound involving the spectral radius, since $\\\\beta=\\\\lambda_1n/(2m)$ and $\\\\beta\\\\geq\\\\epsilon\\\\geq1$. Its resolution is not specified in the source.\"",
    "statement_raw_token_sha256": "321161e67ad655e706ddfd4cf405631fcfa6e923cbc7868edf7028fb8ef6318f",
    "statement_decoded_utf8_sha256": "0bd7ab4f2d361eaad38a2809e33c61cadca6c3eef5ab049d1cf4587ef1d0fb91",
