    "statement_raw_token": "\"Let $H$ be a graph, let $S(H)$ be the set of proper labelings of $H$, and let $T_f(H)$ denote the weighted monotone-path tree associated with $f$. Write $d_{crit}$ for the critical density of $H$ and $bb(T_f(H))$ for the spectral radius of $T_f(H)$. **Uniform Star Decomposition Conjecture.** The critical density satisfies\\n\\n$$\\nd_{crit}=\\\\max_{f\\\\in S(H)}\\\\left\\\\{1-\\\\frac{1}{\\\\lambda(T_f(H))^2}\\\\right\\\\}.\\n$$\\n This is the asserted sharpness of the star-decomposition bound from the preceding corollary; the source supplies no evidence that it has been resolved.\"",
