    "statement_raw_token": "\"Let $K_{n,m}$ be the complete bipartite graph. Denote its critical edge density by $d_{crit}(K_{n,m})=d(n,m)$ and the best edge density obtained from star decomposition by $d_s(n,m)$. **Complete bipartite star-decomposition conjecture.**\\n\\n$$\\nd_{crit}(K_{n,m})=d_s(n,m)=1-\\\\frac{1}{n+m-1}.\\n$$\\n The formula is stated in the complete bipartite graph case, but the source does not provide a resolution status for this conjectural claim.\"",
