    "statement_raw_token": "\"Let $X_\\\\lambda$ be the unipotent $kG$-module labelled by a partition $\\\\lambda\\\\in\\\\mathcal{P}_n$, and let $e$ be the parameter defining the relevant block-theoretic core. An **$e$-core** is the partition obtained from $\\\\lambda$ by removing all possible $e$-hooks, and a **$2$-core** is defined analogously. **2-core conjecture.** If $X_\\\\lambda$ is weakly cuspidal, then the $e$-core of $\\\\lambda$ is a $2$-core.\\nThis is a combinatorial restriction on labels of weakly cuspidal unipotent modules and is presented as a conjecture in the source. Its resolution is not specified.\"",
