    "statement_raw_token": "\"Let $p>2$ be a prime, let $f(x)\\\\in \\\\mathbb{F}_p[x]$ be a non-constant polynomial, and let $\\\\mathcal{S}_{f(x)}^p$ denote the multiplicative semigroup of the quotient ring $\\\\mathbb{F}_p[x]/\\\\langle f(x)\\\\rangle$. Let $U(\\\\mathcal{S}_{f(x)}^p)$ denote its group of units. **Davenport constant equality conjecture.** One has\\n\\n$$\\nD(\\\\mathcal{S}_{f(x)}^p)=D\\\\bigl(U(\\\\mathcal{S}_{f(x)}^p)\\\\bigr).\\n$$\\n\\nThe paper proves this equality when $f(x)$ factors into pairwise non-associated irreducible polynomials, and verifies the special case $f(x)=(x+1)^2$; the general case for non-constant $f(x)$ remains open.\"",
    "statement_raw_token_sha256": "1bb7d194d6de3f2ff145bb3d33f3cebb1ac6cafb7b0ec7a84a51b53a0a9226f8",
