    "statement_raw_token": "\"Let $G$ be a simple undirected graph with $n$ vertices and $\\\\kappa$ connected components. Let $\\\\mu_1\\\\geq\\\\cdots\\\\geq\\\\mu_n$ be the eigenvalues of its adjacency matrix, and let $\\\\pi$ and $\\\\nu$ be the numbers of positive and negative eigenvalues, counted with multiplicity. Define\\n\\n$$\\ns^+=\\\\sum_{i=1}^{\\\\pi}\\\\mu_i^2,\\\\qquad s^-=\\\\sum_{i=n-\\\\nu+1}^{n}\\\\mu_i^2.\\n$$\\n\\n**Componentwise inertia sum-of-squares conjecture.** One has\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\min\\\\{s^-,s^+\\\\}\\\\geq n-\\\\kappa.\\n$$\\n\\nFor a connected graph, this specializes to the conjectured lower bound $\\\\min\\\\{s^-,s^+\\\\}\\\\geq n-1$, and either one-sided inequality implies the corresponding Hong-type bound. The supplied source gives no evidence of a resolution for the general disconnected-graph formulation.\"",
    "statement_raw_token_sha256": "4a1cbd061a36b606d7acad94b2b1a46b8f89e5957918f9f0f9263ca54dc71197",
    "statement_decoded_utf8_sha256": "72b2fb7eefb4dda410e259e8e4b957203b1f769a4e01b4bed9926efcf6771708",
